        "Roman expedition",
        "local Roman veterans"
      ],
      "body": "Twenty Roman veterans make themselves known to Valerius after hearing of his growing influence and the reputation that has followed the expedition through the surrounding territories. They present themselves as men who have served long enough in the region to know its roads, water sources, settlements, seasonal difficulties, and the habits of communities beyond the immediate Roman camps. They ask for no enlistment payment and instead request only that, if accepted, they eventually serve in Valerius's personal guard, where they believe their accumulated experience would be most useful. Valerius refuses to grant that position merely on reputation and tells them that their claim must be demonstrated in the field. The twenty agree to prove their worth before their admission is made permanent.",
