        "Roman expedition",
        "local Roman veterans"
      ],
      "body": "The twenty veterans are given no special privileges during the first stage of their trial. Valerius sends them ahead under observation with the task of identifying practical routes between the expedition's present position and the known sections of the engineered road without relying on the expedition's existing route register. Their value is tested against what they actually know rather than what they claim to know. They identify several usable approaches, distinguish ground that becomes difficult after rain, and point out places where a traveler would naturally seek water. Their information is checked against the expedition's existing observations before any decision is made about their admission.",
