      "date": "19 June 57 BCE",
      "event_category": "Connected",
      "title": "TITUS VARENUS CORRECTS THE COLUMN'S ROUTE ASSUMPTION",
      "mentioned_entities": [
        "Gaius Maximus Valerius",
        "Titus Varenus",
        "Roman expedition",
        "expedition scribes"
      ],
      "body": "During the second stage of the proving exercise, Titus Varenus identifies a route that appears shorter on the expedition's working map but becomes impractical farther ahead. He explains the local ground in terms of an old seasonal drainage path and directs the scouts toward a higher approach that remains passable. The expedition's scribes compare his account with the terrain immediately at hand and find that his warning corresponds with the physical ground. Valerius treats the demonstration as evidence of useful local knowledge rather than as proof that Varenus should command the others. The other veterans remain under the same proving conditions and continue working as a group.",
