      ],
      "body": "Valerius brings the veterans into the expedition's established loose-phalanx drill so that their local experience is tested alongside their ability to function within his existing doctrine. The veterans initially tighten their spacing more than the formation requires, but after instruction they adopt the deliberate intervals and outward-facing watch used by the rest of the column. Their experience proves useful in identifying where the formation can safely pause without losing access to water or obscuring the surrounding approaches. By the end of the exercise, the twenty are no longer being judged simply as men with stories about the territory; they have demonstrated that their knowledge can be integrated into the expedition's actual field method.",
