      "body": "A small detachment of the veterans identifies a secondary water source near an established approach that does not appear in the expedition's existing register. The discovery does not prove that the source is permanent, and the veterans themselves caution that its usefulness depends upon the season. Their warning prevents the expedition from treating the find as a guaranteed supply point. The scribes record both the location as a local reference and the limitation attached to it, preserving the distinction between veteran knowledge and a fully surveyed logistical asset. Valerius orders the source investigated further before it is incorporated into future movement planning.",
